     nothing on it and nothing is what got drawn — so the frame went empty for a stretch of every lap. The grid
     gives the eye the ground and the distance back.

     It belongs to that look and to no other. A grid of glowing lines is what the orange look IS; the same
     geometry in daylight is a set of pale stripes painted across Surfers Paradise, which is nonsense. Rather
